# Purpose

This document defines the overall architecture of the BestWayGrow Franchise subsystem.

The Franchise subsystem provides the operational framework for managing authorized franchise partners who support product distribution, PIN inventory management, customer assistance, financial transactions, and regional business operations.

The Franchise system operates under the Admin governance structure and integrates with Financial, Inventory, Core, User, and Audit systems.

---

# Franchise Role Definition

A Franchise is an authorized business operational unit responsible for:

- PIN purchasing
- Product purchasing
- Inventory management
- Customer support
- Local business operations
- Transaction processing
- Regional service execution

The Franchise does not control enterprise-level financial authority.

All financial operations are governed through:

- System Bank
- Franchise Bank
- Financial Architecture
- Audit System

---

# Franchise Architecture Objectives

The Franchise subsystem is designed to:

- Provide controlled business expansion
- Enable regional operations
- Maintain inventory availability
- Support user services
- Provide transparent financial tracking
- Ensure secure operations
- Maintain complete audit history

